IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Education Services for Overseas Students Act 2000 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the overseas student meets: whether I
-- am an overseas student (s 5); whether the provider may offer me the course (ss 8, 101); how much of my fees it may take before
-- I start (s 27) and whether it must hold them in a protected account (ss 28, 29, 31); what it must report about me and by when
-- (s 19); when my provider defaults and what it must do within 14 days (ss 46A, 46D), the Tuition Protection Service's placement
-- options (s 49) and payment from the Overseas Students Tuition Fund (ss 50A-50C); when I default and the refund I am owed
-- (ss 47A, 47B, 47D, 47E); and recovering it (s 48).
--
-- SEAT: the overseas student, or intending overseas student (s 5). "Is this provider allowed to take me? How much can it ask me
-- to pay up front? What happens to my fees if my course doesn't start, or the provider closes? If I withdraw, what do I get back,
-- and by when?" Duties addressed to the registered provider, the TPS Director and the ESOS agency are encoded as what they mean
-- for the student.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 45, compilation date 5 December 2025, includes amendments up to Act No. 74, 2025 (register id
-- C2025C00684), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00757.txt.
--
-- INPUTS SET OUTSIDE THE ACT. The amount of a refund is set by the written agreement (s 47D) or by the Minister's legislative
-- instruments (ss 46D(7), 47E(4)), none deposited: the amount is not computed. Who holds a "student visa" (defined by the
-- regulations), the kinds of student the regulations exclude, providers the regulations exempt from s 28-29 (s 31(b), (c)),
-- registration on the Register (s 14A), and the "suitable alternative course" criteria (s 49(6)) are asked as facts. The
-- national code (Part 4) is not deposited.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Registration, renewal and its conditions (Part 2); the providers' other duties (ss 15-18, 21-21B, 26) except as
-- noted; the national code; the TPS levies, the OSTF's administration, the TPS Director and the Board (Parts 5A, 5B); sanctions,
-- suspension certificates beyond s 101, monitoring and enforcement (Parts 6-7); review of decisions (Part 7AA: only providers may
-- seek it); offences' penalty amounts (quoted in comments); the machinery (Parts 1, 8). Business days (s 29(2), s 46B(2)) are not
-- counted: the answer names the period.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the overseas student's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Education Services for Overseas Students Act 2000 -- the overseas student's questions`

§§ `s 5 -- am I an overseas student`

-- s 5: "overseas student means a person (whether within or outside Australia) who holds a student visa, but does not include
-- students of a kind prescribed in the regulations." "intending overseas student means a person (whether within or outside
-- Australia) who intends to become, or who has taken any steps towards becoming, an overseas student." "student visa has the
-- meaning given by the regulations" (asked as a fact). Parts 3 and 5 protect both.
DECLARE `Am I protected as an overseas student` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am an overseas student (s 5)`
    `yes: I am an intending overseas student (s 5)`
    `no: I am neither an overseas student nor an intending overseas student`

@export Am I an "overseas student" or "intending overseas student" protected by the ESOS Act (s 5)?
GIVEN `I hold a student visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold an Australian student visa (whether you are in Australia or outside it)
      `I am of a kind the regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a kind of student the ESOS Regulations exclude from "overseas student"
      `I intend to, or have taken steps to, become one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to become, or have taken any steps towards becoming, a student visa holder studying in Australia (for example by applying for a course or a visa)
GIVETH AN `Am I protected as an overseas student`
`Am I an overseas student` MEANS
    IF `I hold a student visa` AND (NOT `I am of a kind the regulations exclude`)
    THEN `yes: I am an overseas student (s 5)`
    ELSE IF `I intend to, or have taken steps to, become one`
         THEN `yes: I am an intending overseas student (s 5)`
         ELSE `no: I am neither an overseas student nor an intending overseas student`

§§ `ss 8, 101 -- may this provider offer me the course`

-- s 8(1): an offence ("Imprisonment for 2 years") for a person who provides a course at a location to an overseas student, or
-- offers or invites one to undertake it, if "(b) the person is not registered to provide that particular course at that
-- particular location". (2): not if done "in accordance with an arrangement that the person has with a registered provider for
-- that particular course for that particular location". s 101(1): an offence to offer, invite or hold out a registered provider
-- "while an Immigration Minister's suspension certificate is in effect for that registered provider". Registration is on the
-- Register (s 14A): a fact.
DECLARE `May this provider offer me the course` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the provider is registered for this course at this location`
    `yes: the provider acts under an arrangement with a provider registered for this course at this location (s 8(2))`
    `no: no one may offer or invite me to this course while an Immigration Minister's suspension certificate is in effect for the provider (s 101)`
    `no: offering me this course would be an offence, because no registered provider for this course at this location stands behind it (s 8(1))`

@export Is this education provider allowed to offer me, as an overseas student, this course at this campus (ss 8, 101)?
GIVEN `the provider is registered for this course at this location` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider is registered (on the CRICOS Register kept under s 14A) to provide this particular course at this particular location
      `it acts under an arrangement with a registered provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not registered itself: whether it offers the course under an arrangement with a provider registered for this course at this location
      `a suspension certificate is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Immigration Minister's suspension certificate is in effect for the registered provider
GIVETH A `May this provider offer me the course`
`May this provider offer me the course (s 8)` MEANS
    IF `a suspension certificate is in effect`
    THEN `no: no one may offer or invite me to this course while an Immigration Minister's suspension certificate is in effect for the provider (s 101)`
    ELSE IF `the provider is registered for this course at this location`
         THEN `yes: the provider is registered for this course at this location`
         ELSE IF `it acts under an arrangement with a registered provider`
              THEN `yes: the provider acts under an arrangement with a provider registered for this course at this location (s 8(2))`
              ELSE `no: offering me this course would be an offence, because no registered provider for this course at this location stands behind it (s 8(1))`

§§ `ss 27, 28, 29, 31 -- my fees before the course starts`

-- s 27(1): "A registered provider must not receive, in respect of an overseas student or intending overseas student, more than
-- 50% of the student's total tuition fees for a course before the student has begun the course." (2): not if "(a) either of the
-- following choose to pay more than 50% ...: (i) the student; (ii) a person who is responsible for paying those fees; or (b) the
-- course has a duration of 25 weeks or less."
DECLARE `How much may my provider take before I start` IS ONE OF
    `no more than` HAS `the amount` IS A NUMBER
    `no limit under s 27: I (or whoever pays my fees) chose to pay more than half`
    `no limit under s 27: the course lasts 25 weeks or less`

@export How much of my tuition fees may my provider take before I start the course (s 27)?
GIVEN `my total tuition fees for the course` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total tuition fees for the whole course, in dollars
      `the course weeks` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks the course lasts
      `I chose to pay more than half` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or the person responsible for paying your fees, chose to pay more than half the fees before you start
GIVETH A `How much may my provider take before I start`
`How much may my provider take before I start` MEANS
    IF `the course weeks` AT MOST 25
    THEN `no limit under s 27: the course lasts 25 weeks or less`
    ELSE IF `I chose to pay more than half`
         THEN `no limit under s 27: I (or whoever pays my fees) chose to pay more than half`
         ELSE `no more than` (`my total tuition fees for the course` TIMES 0.5)

-- ss 28, 29: a registered provider that receives tuition fees before the student has begun must keep "an account" with an
-- Australian ADI and pay the fees into it "within 5 business days" (s 29(2)); "at all times" the account must hold enough "to
-- repay all tuition fees to every overseas student ... who has not yet begun the course" (s 29(3)); withdrawals below that only
-- for a refund, an alternative course or the TPS Director (s 29(4)); and the protected amount "is not available for the payment
-- of a debt of any creditor of the provider" (s 29(6)). s 31: exempt are "(a) a provider that is administered by a State
-- education authority; (b) any other provider that is entitled to receive funds under a law of the Commonwealth for recurrent
-- expenditure for the provision of education or training, other than one excluded by the regulations ...; (c) any other provider
-- specified in the regulations."
@export I paid tuition fees before starting my course. Must my provider keep them in a protected account until I start (ss 28, 29, 31)?
GIVEN `I paid fees before starting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider received tuition fees for you before you began the course
      `I have begun the course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have now begun the course
      `the provider is run by a State education authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider is administered by a State education authority (for example a State government school or TAFE)
      `the provider gets Commonwealth recurrent funding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider is entitled to Commonwealth recurrent funding for education or training (most public universities), and is not excluded by the regulations
      `the provider is exempted by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations specify the provider as exempt from ss 28 and 29
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my provider hold my prepaid fees in a protected account` IF
        `I paid fees before starting`
    AND (NOT `I have begun the course`)
    AND (NOT `the provider is run by a State education authority`)
    AND (NOT `the provider gets Commonwealth recurrent funding`)
    AND (NOT `the provider is exempted by the regulations`)

§§ `s 19 -- what my provider must report about me`

-- s 19(1): the provider "must give the following information within the applicable number of days after the event": "(c) the
-- prescribed information about an accepted student who does not begin his or her course when expected; (d) any termination of
-- an accepted student's studies ... before the student's course is completed; (e) any change in the identity or duration of an
-- accepted student's course". (1A): "(a) if the accepted student is less than 18 years old and the information is of a kind
-- referred to in paragraph (1)(c) or (d)--14 days; or (b) otherwise--31 days." (3): by entering it in the Secretary's computer
-- system (PRISMS, s 109). (2): a breach of a prescribed student visa condition "as soon as practicable". "within ... days after"
-- the event: by the event day plus that number.
DECLARE `What happened` IS ONE OF
    `I did not begin my course when expected`
    `my studies ended before the course was completed`
    `my course, or its length, changed`
    `I was accepted into the course`

@export Something changed in my studies. By when must my provider report it to the Department (s 19)?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened` @desc What happened: you did not start when expected, your studies ended early, your course or its length changed, or you were accepted into the course
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the event happened
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years on that day
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my provider report it` MEANS
    IF     `my age` LESS THAN 18
       AND (   `what happened` EQUALS `I did not begin my course when expected`
            OR `what happened` EQUALS `my studies ended before the course was completed`)
    THEN `the day it happened` PLUS 14
    ELSE `the day it happened` PLUS 31

§§ `ss 46A, 46D, 49, 50A, 50B -- my provider has defaulted`

-- (Situation: my course did not start, or stopped, because of the provider.)
-- s 46A(1): "A registered provider defaults ... if: (a) either of the following occurs: (i) the provider fails to start to provide
-- the course to the student at the location on the agreed starting day; (ii) the course ceases to be provided to the student at
-- the location at any time after it starts but before it is completed; and (b) the student has not withdrawn before the default
-- day." (2): including where "prevented ... because a sanction has been imposed". (3): not if it is "because the student defaults
-- ... under paragraph 47A(1)(c)" (refusal for non-payment, visa breach or misbehaviour). s 5: "agreed starting day ... means the
-- day on which the course was scheduled to start, or a later day agreed"; "default day" is the agreed starting day for (a)(i) and
-- the day the course ceases for (a)(ii).
DECLARE `What went wrong with my course` IS ONE OF
    `the provider did not start my course on the agreed starting day`
    `my course stopped being provided after it started and before I completed it`
    `my course went ahead as agreed`

@export My course did not start, or stopped part-way. Has my provider "defaulted" under the ESOS Act (s 46A)?
GIVEN `what went wrong` IS A `What went wrong with my course` @desc Whether the provider failed to start your course on the agreed starting day, the course stopped before you completed it, or neither
      `I withdrew before the default day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you withdrew from the course before the agreed starting day (or before the day the course stopped)
      `the provider refused me for non-payment, a visa breach or misbehaviour` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the course did not start or stopped for you because the provider refused to teach you for not paying, breaching a student visa condition, or misbehaviour (after giving you natural justice)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my provider defaulted` IF
        (NOT (`what went wrong` EQUALS `my course went ahead as agreed`))
    AND (NOT `I withdrew before the default day`)
    AND (NOT `the provider refused me for non-payment, a visa breach or misbehaviour`)

-- s 46D(2): "The provider must discharge its obligations to the student ... within the period (the provider obligation period) of
-- 14 days after the default day." (3): it does so if "(a) ... the provider arranges for the student to be offered a place in a
-- course in accordance with subsection (4) [an alternative course at the provider's expense]; (ii) the student accepts the offer in
-- writing; or (b) the provider provides a refund in accordance with subsection (6)" -- "of any unspent tuition fees", worked out by
-- the Minister's instrument (s 46D(7), not deposited). s 46B(4): the provider must also notify the student in writing.
-- s 49: if the TPS Director determines the provider has failed (or is unlikely) to discharge its obligations, the TPS Director
-- "must provide ... the student with one or more options for ... alternative courses" if any suitable ones are available; the
-- student's written acceptance must be made within "(a) the period of 30 days after the end of the provider obligation period",
-- or a shorter or (agreed) longer period the TPS Director sets in exceptional circumstances.
-- s 50A(2), (3): a call on the OSTF is made if the provider "has failed to discharge its obligations under section 46D ... by the
-- end of the provider obligation period", whether or not the student accepts a place through s 49; (5): not if the TPS Director
-- "becomes aware" of the circumstances "more than 12 months after the relevant default day". s 50B(1), (3), (4): the TPS Director
-- pays "the amount that the provider must still pay" -- to the new provider if a place is accepted (and any excess over the course
-- cost to the student), otherwise to the student. s 50C(1): the student then "cease[s] to have any claim against the provider".
-- "within 14 days after" and "30 days after": the default day plus 14, and plus 44. "More than 12 months after" the default day:
-- after the same date a year on.
DECLARE `What I get when my provider defaults` IS ONE OF
    `my provider must, by the day given, either arrange a place in another course at its expense that I accept in writing, or refund my unspent tuition fees (s 46D)` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `the provider has met its obligations to me (s 46D(3)); nothing is owed through the Tuition Protection Service`
    `the TPS Director must offer me suitable alternative courses if any are available, which I may accept in writing by the day given, and the Tuition Fund pays the new provider or refunds me; my claim against the old provider ends (ss 49, 50A, 50B, 50C)` HAS `the last day to accept` IS A DATE
    `nothing through the Tuition Protection Service: the TPS Director learned of the default more than 12 months after the default day (s 50A(5)); my claim against the provider remains (s 48)`

@export My provider has defaulted. What must it do for me and by when, and what does the Tuition Protection Service do if it doesn't (ss 46D, 49, 50A)?
GIVEN `the default day` IS A DATE @desc The agreed starting day the course failed to start on, or the day the course stopped being provided
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `the provider has placed or refunded me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 14 days, the provider either refunded your unspent tuition fees or arranged a place in another course at its expense that you accepted in writing
      `the day the TPS Director became aware` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tuition Protection Service Director became aware that the provider may have failed (ignored while the 14 days are running)
GIVETH A `What I get when my provider defaults`
`What do I get when my provider defaults` MEANS
    IF `the provider has placed or refunded me`
    THEN `the provider has met its obligations to me (s 46D(3)); nothing is owed through the Tuition Protection Service`
    ELSE IF `today` AT MOST `the end of the provider obligation period`
         THEN `my provider must, by the day given, either arrange a place in another course at its expense that I accept in writing, or refund my unspent tuition fees (s 46D)` `the end of the provider obligation period`
         ELSE IF `the day the TPS Director became aware` GREATER THAN `twelve months after the default day`
              THEN `nothing through the Tuition Protection Service: the TPS Director learned of the default more than 12 months after the default day (s 50A(5)); my claim against the provider remains (s 48)`
              ELSE `the TPS Director must offer me suitable alternative courses if any are available, which I may accept in writing by the day given, and the Tuition Fund pays the new provider or refunds me; my claim against the old provider ends (ss 49, 50A, 50B, 50C)` (`the end of the provider obligation period` PLUS 30)
    WHERE
        `the end of the provider obligation period` MEANS `the default day` PLUS 14
        `twelve months after the default day` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY `the default day`) (DATE_MONTH `the default day`) (DATE_YEAR `the default day` PLUS 1)

§§ `ss 47A, 47B, 47D, 47E, 48, 50A(4) -- I have withdrawn, not started, or been refused`

-- s 47A(1): "An overseas student or intending overseas student defaults ... if: (a) the course starts at the location on the
-- agreed starting day, but the student does not start the course on that day (and has not previously withdrawn); or (b) the
-- student withdraws from the course ... (either before or after the agreed starting day); or (c) the registered provider ...
-- refuses to provide, or continue providing, the course to the student ... because of ...: (i) the student failed to pay an
-- amount ...; (ii) the student breached a condition of his or her student visa; (iii) misbehaviour by the student." (2): not
-- under (a) if the student did not start because the provider defaulted. (3): not under (c)(iii) "unless the registered provider
-- accords the student natural justice". s 5 "default day": (a) the agreed starting day; (b) the day of withdrawal; (c) the day of
-- the refusal.
DECLARE `What I did, or what was done to me` IS ONE OF
    `the course started on the agreed day but I did not start it`
    `I withdrew from the course`
    `the provider refused to teach me because I did not pay`
    `the provider refused to teach me because I breached a student visa condition`
    `the provider refused to teach me for misbehaviour`

DECLARE `Have I defaulted` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I have defaulted (s 47A), and the default day is` HAS `the default day` IS A DATE
    `no: I did not start because the provider defaulted, so it is the provider's default (s 47A(2), s 46A)`
    `no: a refusal for misbehaviour is not my default unless the provider first gave me natural justice (s 47A(3))`

@export I did not start, withdrew from, or was refused my course. Have I "defaulted" under the ESOS Act, and on what day (s 47A)?
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I did, or what was done to me` @desc Which happened: you did not start a course that started on the agreed day, you withdrew, or the provider refused to teach you for non-payment, a visa breach or misbehaviour
      `the agreed starting day` IS A DATE @desc The day the course was scheduled to start, or a later day you and the provider agreed
      `the day I withdrew or was refused` IS A DATE @desc The day you withdrew, or the day the provider refused to provide (or continue) the course (ignored for not starting)
      `I did not start because the provider defaulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not start because the provider failed to start the course on the agreed day
      `I was given natural justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a refusal for misbehaviour: whether the provider gave you natural justice (a fair hearing) before refusing
GIVETH A `Have I defaulted`
`Have I defaulted (s 47A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `the course started on the agreed day but I did not start it` THEN
        IF `I did not start because the provider defaulted`
        THEN `no: I did not start because the provider defaulted, so it is the provider's default (s 47A(2), s 46A)`
        ELSE `yes: I have defaulted (s 47A), and the default day is` `the agreed starting day`
    WHEN `the provider refused to teach me for misbehaviour` THEN
        IF `I was given natural justice`
        THEN `yes: I have defaulted (s 47A), and the default day is` `the day I withdrew or was refused`
        ELSE `no: a refusal for misbehaviour is not my default unless the provider first gave me natural justice (s 47A(3))`
    OTHERWISE `yes: I have defaulted (s 47A), and the default day is` `the day I withdrew or was refused`

-- s 47B: the provider "must enter into a written agreement with each [student] that: (a) sets out the refund requirements that
-- apply if the student defaults ...; and (b) meets the requirements (if any) set out in the national code."
-- s 47D(2)-(4): it must pay "the amount (if any) required by the agreement", to the student or a person the agreement specifies,
-- "within the period (the provider obligation period) of 4 weeks after receiving a written claim from the student". (5): not
-- required if "(a) the student was refused a student visa; and (b) the refusal was a reason for" not starting, withdrawing or not
-- paying. s 47E(1): a refund is owed under s 47E instead if the provider "has not entered into an agreement ... that meets the
-- requirements of section 47B" or s 47D(5) applies; (2): the amount by the Minister's instrument (s 47E(4), not deposited); (3):
-- "within the period ... of 4 weeks after the default day". s 48: "may recover an amount owing ... as a debt by action in a court";
-- the specified person for a s 47D refund. s 50A(4): if the provider does not pay by the end of the provider obligation period, a
-- call is made on the OSTF (unless the TPS Director learns of it more than 12 months after the default day, s 50A(5)). 4 weeks is
-- 28 days.
DECLARE `My refund after my default` IS ONE OF
    `a refund of the amount my written agreement sets, to me or the person it names, within 4 weeks after my written claim: by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `a refund of the amount the Minister's instrument sets, to me, within 4 weeks after the default day: by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

@export I have defaulted on my course. What refund must my provider pay, to whom, and by when (ss 47D, 47E)?
GIVEN `the default day` IS A DATE @desc Your default day (the agreed starting day if you did not start; otherwise the day you withdrew or were refused)
      `I have a written agreement that meets s 47B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the provider signed a written agreement setting out the refunds if you default, meeting the national code's requirements
      `I was refused a student visa, which caused it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were refused a student visa and that refusal was a reason you did not start, withdrew, or did not pay
      `the day of my written claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the provider received your written claim for the refund (only matters under a written agreement)
GIVETH A `My refund after my default`
`What refund must my provider pay after my default` MEANS
    IF `I have a written agreement that meets s 47B` AND (NOT `I was refused a student visa, which caused it`)
    THEN `a refund of the amount my written agreement sets, to me or the person it names, within 4 weeks after my written claim: by` (`the day of my written claim` PLUS 28)
    ELSE `a refund of the amount the Minister's instrument sets, to me, within 4 weeks after the default day: by` (`the default day` PLUS 28)

-- s 50A(4), (5); s 50B(1), (3); s 48(1).
DECLARE `If my refund is not paid` IS ONE OF
    `the provider has paid the refund: nothing more is owed under Division 2`
    `the refund is not overdue yet: the provider still has until the last day`
    `the TPS Director must pay me the refund from the Overseas Students Tuition Fund (or the person my agreement names), and my claim against the provider ends (ss 50A(4), 50B, 50C)`
    `nothing through the Tuition Protection Service: the TPS Director learned of it more than 12 months after the default day (s 50A(5)); I may sue the provider for it as a debt (s 48)`

@export My provider has not paid the refund I am owed after my default. Will the Tuition Protection Service pay me (s 50A(4))?
GIVEN `the default day` IS A DATE @desc Your default day
      `the last day for the refund` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the provider's 4 weeks to pay (from the previous question)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `the provider has paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider has paid the refund
      `the day the TPS Director became aware` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tuition Protection Service Director became aware the refund may not have been paid
GIVETH A `If my refund is not paid`
`Will the Tuition Protection Service pay my refund` MEANS
    IF `the provider has paid`
    THEN `the provider has paid the refund: nothing more is owed under Division 2`
    ELSE IF `today` AT MOST `the last day for the refund`
         THEN `the refund is not overdue yet: the provider still has until the last day`
         ELSE IF `the day the TPS Director became aware` GREATER THAN (Date (DATE_DAY `the default day`) (DATE_MONTH `the default day`) (DATE_YEAR `the default day` PLUS 1))
              THEN `nothing through the Tuition Protection Service: the TPS Director learned of it more than 12 months after the default day (s 50A(5)); I may sue the provider for it as a debt (s 48)`
              ELSE `the TPS Director must pay me the refund from the Overseas Students Tuition Fund (or the person my agreement names), and my claim against the provider ends (ss 50A(4), 50B, 50C)`
